cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantization × Memorization & Factuality"
abstract: >-
  A multi-model study measuring whether INT4/INT8 quantization changes what a
  language model memorizes and how reliably it recalls facts. Across six models,
  INT4 leaves factual accuracy statistically unchanged (replicated null), while
  memorization is driven by model scale rather than precision.
type: software
